GRE_Q.solution:
To determine if the measure of each interior angle is greater than 120 degrees, we can use the formula for the interior angle of a polygon given by the number of sides \text{n}: \text{Interior Angle} = \frac{(n - 2) \times 180}{n}. \text{From Statement (2), we know } n = 9. \text{Thus, the interior angle is} \frac{(9 - 2) \times 180}{9} = \frac{7 \times 180}{9} = 140 \text{ degrees. Since } 140 > 120, \text{ Statement (2) alone is sufficient. }
\text{Statement (1) gives only the sum of the angles, which is insufficient alone. Therefore, }
the correct answer is B: "Statement (2) ALONE is sufficient, but statement (1) alone is not sufficient.".
